SETUP

Install Gradle

In root dir `tracking_tests`, use gradle to generate the project
`gradle init \
--type java-library \
--dsl groovy \
--test-framework junit-jupiter \
--package app \
--project-name tracking_tests`

Gradle generates a whole java project, including folder for application folder for testing code. Ignore the folder for application code  Use only the `test/java/app` part
```
tracking_tests/       ← Gradle testing project
│   ├── settings.gradle
│   ├── build.gradle
│   ├── gradlew
│   ├── gradle/
│   └── src/
│       └── main/java/app/  ← application implementation
│           └── 
|       └── test/java/app/  ← testing code
│           └── 
```

configure `build.gradle` to directly access some source code from the existing implementation. 
```
sourceSets {
    main {
        java {
            srcDirs = ['../src']
            include 'app/Marker.java'
            include 'app/TrackedMarker.java'
            include 'app/MarkerTracker.java'
        }
    }
}
```
